# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# earnyourbeers — onboarded 2026-10-16 at James's earnyourbeers#1
#
#   "Let's migrate this to a react frontend dotnet backend just like the
#   template. This can be kit managed. We can have username auth to keep it
#   simple. It can use a db." … "Onboard the app by finding any spec you can
#   find and creating kit spec. Make inferred spec as well."
#
# Read at earnyourbeers@main 4b6e4f4: a single-user, offline Flutter app,
# branded "Earn Your Vices" in the UI. Its docs/ are mostly brainstorms, so the
# CODE is the reference implementation the web rebuild has to match.
#
#   DEFINED   — his words on earnyourbeers#1, or a doc that describes what the
#               code also does. Cites the issue or the doc.
#   INFERRED  — a rule only the Dart code states. Cites file:line (or a test).
#               Each is `review unreviewed`: it shows in Proposed, and he can
#               deny it. Numbers are copied from the code, not from the docs,
#               which disagree with it (see BEH-SCORE-1).
#
# ⚠️ Nothing here is built for the web yet. Every behaviour describes the app
# the rebuild must reproduce, plus the account layer the web adds.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

feature FEAT-ACCOUNT "Accounts (new for the web)"
feature FEAT-LOG "Logging activities and vices"
feature FEAT-BALANCE "The weekly balance"
feature FEAT-LEAGUE "Leagues and weekly settlement"
feature FEAT-ONBOARD "Onboarding"
feature FEAT-SETTINGS "Settings"


# ═══ DEFINED — earnyourbeers#1 ═══

behaviour BEH-WEB-1 "Earn Your Vices is a website: a React frontend on a .NET backend, like web-template"
  in FEAT-ACCOUNT
  layer technical
  source defined earnyourbeers#1
  priority 1
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Dashboard
  then sees region:Balance
  contract the Flutter app is the reference implementation, not the product: the web app replaces it
  contract state lives in a server database, not on the device

behaviour BEH-AUTH-1 "A person signs up and signs in with a username and password"
  in FEAT-ACCOUNT
  layer ux
  source defined earnyourbeers#1
  priority 1
  actor athlete
  when opens page:SignIn
  when fills field:Username with ?username
  when fills field:Password with ?password
  when activates button:SignIn
  then sees page:Dashboard
  contract "username auth to keep it simple": no email, no social login, no password reset by email

# The shape I chose for his "username auth" (earnyourbeers#7). Auth stays his to merge, so
# this sits in Proposed until he approves or denies it.
behaviour BEH-AUTH-3 "Usernames are 3 to 32 characters, passwords at least 8, and a session lasts 30 days"
  in FEAT-ACCOUNT
  layer technical
  source defined earnyourbeers#7
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor athlete
  contract a username is letters, digits, dot, underscore or hyphen, unique ignoring case
  contract passwords are stored as PBKDF2-SHA256 hashes, never as text
  contract the session is an HTTP-only SameSite=Lax cookie that slides for 30 days
  contract a wrong password and an unknown username fail with the same message

behaviour BEH-AUTH-2 "Each person's logs, league and settings are their own"
  in FEAT-ACCOUNT
  layer technical
  source defined earnyourbeers#1
  priority 1
  actor athlete
  given account:Other
  when opens page:Dashboard
  then sees region:Balance
  contract every row the app stores belongs to one user, and no route returns another user's rows
  contract the device-local app had no user at all, so this is the one rule the rebuild adds rather than ports


# ═══ INFERRED — what the Flutter code does today ═══

behaviour BEH-SCORE-1 "Activities earn points: run 0.5 a km, cycle 1/6 a km, swim 1/60 a length"
  in FEAT-BALANCE
  layer technical
  source inferred lib/core/logic/pint_calculator.dart:13
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor athlete
  provides activity:Run.pointsPerKm = 0.5
  provides activity:Cycle.pointsPerKm = 1/6
  provides activity:Swim.pointsPerLength = 1/60
  contract an unknown activity type earns nothing
  contract test/pint_calculator_test.dart still expects 3, 1 and 0.1 and the README says 1 pint = 5 km run; the code's numbers win here

behaviour BEH-SCORE-2 "Activity points are scaled by the league's difficulty; a vice always costs 1 point"
  in FEAT-BALANCE
  layer technical
  source inferred lib/core/logic/pint_calculator.dart:48
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor athlete
  contract balance = (sum of activity points × difficulty) − (sum of vice units)
  contract difficulty = 10 × 0.794328^level (app_state.dart:268): 10× at tier 0, about 1× at tier 10, 0.1× at tier 20

behaviour BEH-BALANCE-1 "The dashboard shows this week's balance to 2dp, as credit, debt, or square"
  in FEAT-BALANCE
  layer ux
  source inferred lib/ui/screens/dashboard_screen.dart:290
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Dashboard
  then sees region:Balance
  provides region:Balance.states = credit, debt, square
  contract a week runs Monday 00:00 to Monday 00:00 UTC, and the balance counts that week's logs only
  contract UTC is an assumption (earnyourbeers#6): the phone app used local time, and the web has no phone
  contract the number is followed by the vice emoji; the label reads POINTS IN CREDIT, POINTS IN DEBT, or SQUARE at exactly 0

behaviour BEH-LOG-1 "One tap logs one unit: a vice, a km run, a km cycled, or a length swum"
  in FEAT-LOG
  layer ux
  source inferred lib/ui/screens/dashboard_screen.dart:844
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Dashboard
  when activates button:LogRun
  then sees region:Balance
  contract each activity button shows how many points one unit earns at the current tier
  contract tapping the vice card logs 1; a long press asks for an amount, which must be above 0

behaviour BEH-LOG-2 "Repeat taps within an hour add to the latest entry instead of making a new one"
  in FEAT-LOG
  layer technical
  source inferred lib/core/logic/app_state.dart:486
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor athlete
  contract only the newest entry of all is checked: same activity type, or a vice after a vice, logged under 1 hour ago

behaviour BEH-LOG-3 "Only the newest entry this week can be edited or deleted"
  in FEAT-LOG
  layer ux
  source inferred lib/ui/screens/dashboard_screen.dart:368
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Dashboard
  then sees region:LogList
  contract an edit accepts 0 or more; anything else closes the dialog without saving

behaviour BEH-HISTORY-1 "Past weeks can be paged through, back to the first log"
  in FEAT-BALANCE
  layer ux
  source inferred test/dashboard_interaction_test.dart:Weekly History Swipe Navigation
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Dashboard
  then sees region:WeekHeader
  contract headers read CURRENT WEEK or WEEK OF d/m; each entry shows its amount and "Logged at H:MM"
  contract a past week's balance uses TODAY's difficulty, not the one in force that week

behaviour BEH-LEAGUE-1 "There are 20 tiers in four divisions, and the banner shows where you are"
  in FEAT-LEAGUE
  layer ux
  source inferred lib/core/logic/app_state.dart:23
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Dashboard
  then sees region:LeagueBanner
  contract divisions are Apprenticeship, Practice, Mastery and Legacy, five tiers each
  contract the banner shows the division, the tier name, and the tally to 2dp on a bar from −25 to +25

behaviour BEH-SETTLE-1 "Each new week settles the last: its net balance moves the tally, and the tally moves the tier"
  in FEAT-LEAGUE
  layer technical
  source inferred test/league_settlement_test.dart:single promotion at +25 points
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor athlete
  contract tally ≥ 50: up two tiers and −50; tally ≥ 25: up one and −25; tally ≤ −25: down one and +25; otherwise it carries over
  contract the tier is clamped to the list; several missed weeks settle as one
  contract the first ever run records the date and settles nothing

behaviour BEH-SETTLE-2 "Settlement is shown as a report you must dismiss before the new week starts"
  in FEAT-LEAGUE
  layer ux
  source inferred lib/ui/dialogs/weekly_settlement_dialog.dart:98
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Dashboard
  then sees region:SettlementReport
  when activates button:StartNewWeek
  then sees region:Balance
  provides region:SettlementReport.states = promoted, double promotion, demoted, position secured
  contract the native app ran settlement on launch; the web runs it on the first request of a new week (an assumption)

behaviour BEH-ONBOARD-1 "Onboarding asks for a sport, a weekly volume, a vice, and a weekly vice count"
  in FEAT-ONBOARD
  layer ux
  source inferred lib/ui/screens/onboarding_screen.dart:86
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Onboarding
  when activates button:Sport
  when fills field:WeeklyVolume with ?volume
  when fills field:Vice with ?emoji
  when fills field:WeeklyVices with ?count
  when activates button:EnterTheArena
  then sees page:Dashboard
  contract volume slider maxes: 100 km run, 300 km cycle, 3000 lengths swim; vices 0 to 40 a week

behaviour BEH-ONBOARD-2 "The answers seed the starting tier"
  in FEAT-ONBOARD
  layer technical
  source inferred lib/ui/screens/onboarding_screen.dart:471
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor athlete
  contract weekly points at tier 0 = volume × base rate × 10; tier = round(ln(points / 25) / 0.23025), clamped 0 to 20
  contract if points − vices < −15 the tier drops by 5, floored at 0
  contract the step bands in app_state.dart:438 are dead code and are not ported

behaviour BEH-VICE-1 "The vice is any single emoji, pizza by default"
  in FEAT-SETTINGS
  layer ux
  source inferred test/rebrand_flow_test.dart:defaults to Pizza emoji
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Settings
  when fills field:Vice with ?emoji
  then sees region:Balance
  contract at most 2 characters, no plain text; empty falls back to 🍕
  contract docs/compliance_strategy.md: the neutral default is the App Store defence, which matters less on the web

behaviour BEH-THEME-1 "The theme is auto, light, or dark"
  in FEAT-SETTINGS
  layer ui
  pending
  source inferred test/rebrand_flow_test.dart:updates theme mode
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Settings
  when activates button:Theme
  provides button:Theme.states = auto, light, dark
  contract accent 0xFFF28E1C on a 0xFF1A1A1A dark surface (lib/ui/theme.dart)

behaviour BEH-RESET-1 "A person can wipe their data and start onboarding again"
  in FEAT-SETTINGS
  layer ux
  source inferred lib/core/logic/app_state.dart:468
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor athlete
  when opens page:Settings
  when activates button:Reset
  then sees page:Onboarding
  contract the native app asks for no confirmation; the web asks once (an assumption)


# ═══ DOCUMENTED, NOT BUILT ═══
#
# Brainstorms in docs/ the code never reached. Kept as one line each so they
# are a list rather than a feeling; none is planned. Wearable sync
# (Strava, Garmin, Apple Health, README.md) is the one a website changes the
# cost of: Strava has a web API; Apple Health has none.
#   docs/leagues_progression.md — a 12-tier "Master Brewer" track per discipline
#   docs/progression_brainstorm.md — "The Path of Discipline" progression themes
#   docs/banking_philosophy.md, docs/debt_mechanics.md — a vault and a debt floor
#   docs/premium_ui_ideas.md, docs/lovable_comparison.md — UI polish ideas
#   docs/pivot.md — "Run for Fun", several reward categories
